Subject: [PATCH] misc: fastrpc: keep userspace invocation waiters across system sleep

Keep the original context in the completion wait across freezing. Ordinary
signals remain interruptible and kernel invocations keep the bounded wait.

OEM: MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource, liuqin-t-oss
     eb49e10028e27fa98856cb5e458c0f0ec5b4554e, drivers/char/adsprpc.c.
     On restart, context_restore_interrupted() recovers the user's
     invocation and the driver rejoins its wait without resubmitting it.
     The Linux freezer-aware wait preserves that context across suspend.

diff --git a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
index adc6f850e..0a0dd9f94 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -1328,7 +1328,9 @@ static inline int fastrpc_wait_for_response(struct fastrpc_invoke_ctx *ctx,
 		if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&ctx->work, 10 * HZ))
 			err = -ETIMEDOUT;
 	} else {
-		err = wait_for_completion_interruptible(&ctx->work);
+		/* Freeze in place without restarting an already submitted RPC. */
+		err = wait_for_completion_state(&ctx->work,
+						TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE | TASK_FREEZABLE);
 	}
 
 	return err;
